WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:05.670
 Sleep is the elixir of life.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.810
But we are a chronically
sleep deprived society.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.990
And studies have shown us
that one in three people

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.420
don't get enough sleep.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.940
As a neuroscientist
at UC Berkeley,

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.060
I am passionate about sleep.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.850
So I have a mission.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:29.010
I desperately want to reunite
humanity with Mother Nature's

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.070
best effort yet at immortality.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.290
We often think of sleep as the
third pillar of good health

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.330
alongside diet and exercise.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.020
But in truth, sleep is
actually the foundation

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:50.330
on which those two
other pillars will sit.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.600
I'm going to share with
you the science behind what

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.330
will enhance your sleep,
why it's important,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.860
and how proper sleep
can benefit your life.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.120
In the brain during deep
sleep, hundreds of thousands

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.200
of brain cells in your cortex
fire together and then they all

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.620
go silent together.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.910
In fact, some parts of
your brain are up to 30%

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:20.350
more active when you go into REM
sleep than when you are awake.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:25.600
Your brain and your body need
to drop their core temperature

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.040
in order for you to fall asleep
and then stay asleep soundly

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.570
across the night.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:38.230
So set your bedroom temperature
to about 68 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:42.760
And using sleep trackers, it
gives us a historical record

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.010
of our sleep, and
they may become

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:49.630
the ultimate secret
sleep weapon.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:54.250
I believe it is time
to reclaim our right

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:59.250
to a full night of sleep and the
opportunity for a better life.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.810
It is never too late to
start sleeping better.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.890
I'm Matthew Walker, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.040
[MUSIC PLAYING]

